  "id": "analog",
  "term": "analog",
  "definition": "In this context, an analog is a real-world setting used as a close stand-in for another environment because it reproduces important features of it. For example, Antarctic research stations can serve as an analog for long-duration space missions because they share isolation, confinement, harsh conditions, and similar demands on group functioning.",
